To exploit the KRACK vulnerability, you must first understand its mechanism: this is a MAC spoofing attack that targets Wi-Fi chips. Your device sends a probe packet to an access point with a forged MAC address. The access point then broadcasts frames with the spoofed MAC address, tricking the network's authentication layer into accepting those frames as legitimate traffic.

